INT. REGIONAL SWIM CENTER - POOL DECK - EARLY MORNING

Chlorine haze. Lane ropes bobbing. Rows of empty bleachers. A single swimmer cuts lengths in lane four.

COACH MARISOL TREVELYAN-ADEWALE (50s, whistle, towel round her neck) crouches at the pool edge with a stopwatch. On the starting block, soaked, goggles pushed up on her forehead, waits ISAURA PRZYBYLSKI-MBEKI (17, racing suit, shoulders too narrow for her ambitions).

MARISOL
Again.

ISAURA
I just did two hundred.

MARISOL
And you'll do another.

ISAURA
Coach.

MARISOL
Isaura.

ISAURA
My arms are lead.

MARISOL
Lead floats if you move fast enough.

Isaura laughs, breath ragged. Lowers her goggles.

MARISOL (CONT'D)
On my whistle.

ISAURA
On your whistle.

Marisol raises it.

MARISOL
Go.

Isaura launches. The water folds around her. Marisol clicks the watch. Walks the deck beside the lane, keeping pace.

At the wall, Isaura tumbles, pushes off. Marisol bends lower.

MARISOL (CONT'D)
Long. Long.

ISAURA (O.S.)
(gasping)
I'm trying!

MARISOL
Long, Isaura!

Isaura touches the far wall. Surfaces. Breathes. Marisol stops the watch. Looks at it.

MARISOL (CONT'D)
Better.

ISAURA
How much?

MARISOL
Two-tenths.

ISAURA
That's all?

MARISOL
That's everything.

Isaura grins. Pulls herself onto the deck and sits, legs dangling. Marisol sits beside her. They both stare at the water.

ISAURA
Can I ask something?

MARISOL
You can ask.

ISAURA
Did you ever want to quit?

MARISOL
Every day.

ISAURA
But you didn't.

MARISOL
I got up. That's the whole trick.

ISAURA
That's not a trick. That's just getting up.

MARISOL
Yes. Exactly.

They say the next line together.

MARISOL ^
Again?

ISAURA
Again.

They laugh. Isaura stands. Marisol rises. The water settles into stillness, waiting for them.
